#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# together

#% text
# `together(e)` writes a sum of fractions as one fraction over a common denominator, in lowest terms.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Common factors of the numerator and the denominator cancel.

#% item
# Functions such as `sin(x)` are treated as variables.

#% item
# `together` maps over lists.

#% item
# Powers with fractional or symbolic exponents are not brought together.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% text
# Two fractions over a common denominator:

#% cell
together(1/x + 1/y)
#% output
#= (x + y)/x/y

#% cell
together(1/(x - 1) - 1/(x + 1))
#% output
#= 2/(-1 + x^2)

#% text
# Common factors cancel:

#% cell
together((x^2 - 1)/(x - 1))
#% output
#= 1 + x

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Several variables:

#% cell
together(a/b + c/d)
#% output
#= (a*d + b*c)/b/d

#% cell
together(1/(a + b) + 1/(a - b))
#% output
#= 2*a/(-b^2 + a^2)

#% text
# A polynomial plus fractions:

#% cell
together(1 + 1/x + 1/x^2)
#% output
#= (1 + x + x^2)*x^-2

#% text
# Functions as variables:

#% cell
together(sin(x) + 1/sin(x))
#% output
#= (1 + sin(x)^2)/sin(x)

#% text
# A list:

#% cell
together([1/x + 1, 1/y + 1])
#% output
#= [(1 + x)/x, (1 + y)/y]

#% text
# Inexact coefficients:

#% cell
together(1.5/x + 1/y)
#% output
#= (x + 1.5*y)/x/y

#% subsection
# Applications

#% text
# Simplify a sum of fractions that cancels down:

#% cell
together(x/(x^2 - 1) + 1/(x + 1))
#% output
#= (-1 + 2*x)/(-1 + x^2)

#% text
# The numerator of the combined fraction, to find where it vanishes:

#% cell
numerator(together(x + 1/x - 5/2))
#% output
#= 2 + -5*x + 2*x^2

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# `apart` splits the fraction again:

#% cell
together(1/x - 1/(x + 1))
#% output
#= (x + x^2)^-1

#% cell
apart(together(1/x - 1/(x + 1)))
#% output
#= -(1 + x)^-1 + x^-1

#% text
# `cancel` puts each term in lowest terms without a common denominator:

#% cell
cancel((x^2 - 1)/(x - 1) + 1/x)
#% output
#= 1 + x + x^-1

#% subsection
# Possible issues

#% text
# Powers with fractional exponents stay apart:

#% cell
together(sqrt(x) + 1/sqrt(x))
#% output
#= x^(-1/2) + x^(1/2)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `apart`, `cancel`, `factor`, `numerator`, `denominator`, `simplify`
